Package: nettact-agent
Version: @VERSION@
Depends: libc, ca-bundle
Source: https://github.com/nettact/agent
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: NetTact <support@nettact.org>
Architecture: all
Description: NetTact monitoring agent for OpenWrt.
 Runs network probes on the router and pushes the results to a NetTact server.
 .
 The package contains no executable: the agent binary is ~11 MB and is
 downloaded on first start instead, either into RAM on every boot or once onto
 the overlay (see the 'mode' option in /etc/config/nettact). One package
 therefore serves every CPU architecture, and an 8 MB router can run the agent
 without spending any flash on it.
 .
 Configure it under Services -> NetTact in LuCI, or in /etc/config/nettact.
